> Wasn't CGA 320x192?  

It was 320x200 when using 4-colour mode, and 640x200 in monochrome. The
character generator used 8x8 cells, which allowed both 40x25 and 80x25
text modes (with all 16 colours). EGA was 640x350, and I think that some
bizzare graphics cards (such as the one in the Tandy 2000) used 640x400
(as could some VGA cards).

I remember this from trying to program the CRT controller in old CGA and
Hercules cards to see what kind of video modes I could get that IBM
didn't think of (or was too afraid to use). I'm surprised I don't have
more dead monitors here...

